f=\"/w/cpp/ranges/random_access_range\"><span class=\"kw2924\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">random_access_range</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> and <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/sized_range\"><span class=\"kw2918\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">sized_range</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span></code> are satisfied,\n</li><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/common_iterator\"><span class=\"kw3138\">std::<span class=\"me2\">common_iterator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2908\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">iterator_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>, <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/iterator_t\"><span class=\"kw2909\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">sentinel_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/begin\"><span class=\"kw2900\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">begin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>base_<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> otherwise.\n</li></ul>\nHere <code><i>base_</i></code> (the name is for exposition only purposes) is the underlying view.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Same as <span class=\"t-v\">(1)</span>, but <code>V</code> is const-qualified.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>An iterator to the beginning of the underlying view.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;numeric&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;ranges&gt;</span>\n<span class=\